---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="Ethnoir helps people navigating ventures and organizations shaping entrepreneurship make sense of current conditions."
>
  <!-- CHAPTER 01: ARRIVE -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter" style="padding-top: var(--space-lg); padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="registration">01</div>
      <div style="max-width: 800px; padding-right: var(--space-lg);">
        <h1 class="voice-1" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md); padding-right: var(--space-xl); font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); line-height: 1.05;">
          Better venture decisions<br/>begin with understanding<br/>what is actually happening.
        </h1>
        <p class="voice-2">
          Ethnoir helps people navigating ventures and organizations shaping entrepreneurship make sense of current conditions, clarify what matters and make better-informed decisions about direction and support.
        </p>
        <div class="actions-group" style="flex-wrap: wrap;">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary" style="background: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain); border-color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">
            Discuss a venture-development challenge
          </a>
          <a href="/venture-readiness-check-in" class="link-secondary">
            Explore the Check-In &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="align-self: start; text-align: left;">
        <div class="editorial-image-container" style="position: relative; z-index: 10;">
          <img src="/images/hero.jpg" alt="A subtle, abstract frosted glass sculpture refracting light" class="editorial-image" style="aspect-ratio: 4/5; object-fit: cover; object-position: center;" />
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: calc(-1 * var(--space-lg)); margin-left: calc(-1 * var(--space-md)); position: relative; z-index: 20; background: var(--color-parchment); padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-sm); width: fit-content;">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--color-deep-body);">
            People.<br/>
            Ventures.<br/>
            <span style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-style: italic; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">What comes next.</span>
          </p>
          <div style="width: 40px; height: 1px; background: var(--color-quiet-rule); margin-top: var(--space-md);"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 02: WHY THIS WORK MATTERS -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing">
    <div class="container two-columns">
      <div>
        <span class="voice-3">Why this work matters</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1">
          The same answer does not fit every venture.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div style="padding-top: var(--space-md);">
        <p class="voice-2">
          A new possibility, an operating business and a venture facing a major change may need very different things. Even ventures at a similar stage can have different goals, constraints and definitions of progress.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">
          Ethnoir looks beyond a <span style="display:inline-block; margin: 0 4px;">single score</span>, <span style="display:inline-block; margin: 0 4px;">stage</span> or <span style="display:inline-block; margin: 0 4px;">standard formula</span>. We consider what is happening, where the venture is trying to go and which conditions matter to the decision at hand.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2">
          The goal is not to prescribe one path. It is to create a clearer basis for deciding what makes sense next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 03: TWO ARENAS -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-moderate-spacing">
    <div class="container two-columns">
      <div class="thin-rule-y" style="padding-right: var(--space-lg);">
        <span class="voice-3">For people navigating ventures</span>
        <p class="voice-2">
          When customers, revenue, operations, finances and competing priorities all demand attention, it can be difficult to see what matters most.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2">
          Ethnoir helps people examine current conditions and consider what may deserve attention next.
        </p>
        <div style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
          <a href="/venture-readiness-check-in" class="link-secondary">Explore the Venture Readiness Check-In</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="voice-3">For organizations shaping entrepreneurship</span>
        <p class="voice-2">
          Programs, resources and opportunities are more useful when they respond to the people and ventures they are intended to support.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2">
          Ethnoir works with relevant organizations to examine venture conditions and questions arising from how entrepreneurship support is designed, delivered or directed.
        </p>
        <div class="subtle-top-rule">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
            Not every venture needs the same next step. Ethnoir uses diagnostic and implementation-focused approaches and is developing an institutional application designed to help organizations understand participant needs and consider how support is placed or routed. That application remains to be tested with a partner organization.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">
          <a href="/for-organizations" class="link-secondary">For Organizations</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 04: HOW ETHNOIR CONTRIBUTES -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-large-spacing">
    <div class="container two-columns">
      <div>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="max-width: 500px;">
          From scattered information to clearer judgment
        </h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">
          Ethnoir brings together relevant information, identifies patterns and gaps, and helps turn what is learned into a clearer basis for judgment.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding-top: var(--space-xs);">
        <div class="thin-rule-x" style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); align-items: baseline;">
          <span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">01</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: 0;">Interpreting current venture conditions</p>
        </div>
        <div class="thin-rule-x" style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); align-items: baseline;">
          <span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">02</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: 0;">Helping people consider what may deserve attention next</p>
        </div>
        <div class="thin-rule-x" style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); align-items: baseline;">
          <span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">03</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: 0;">Designing structured founder support</p>
        </div>
        <div class="thin-rule-x" style="display: flex; gap: var(--space-md); align-items: baseline;">
          <span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">04</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: 0;">Learning from Ethnoir’s own venture-development work</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 05: EVIDENCE -->
  <section class="bg-quiet-sand chapter chapter-large-spacing">
    <div class="container">
      
      <!-- Narrative Anchor -->
      <div style="max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <span class="voice-3">Evidence of current work</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          The Venture Readiness Lab
        </h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">
          In 2026, Ethnoir designed and delivered a six-week pilot for founders working through operational, revenue, financial and implementation questions in their businesses.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Architectural Stats Grid -->
      <div class="stats-grid" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        <div class="stat-block">
          <div class="stat-huge">06</div>
          <div class="stat-caption">weeks</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-block">
          <div class="stat-huge">06</div>
          <div class="stat-caption">active founders</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-block">
          <div class="stat-huge">05</div>
          <div class="stat-caption">participants with structural deliverables independently reviewed</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Architecturally Centered Conclusion Block -->
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; text-align: center;">
        <!-- Vertical Plumb Line -->
        <div style="width: 1px; height: 80px; background-color: var(--color-quiet-rule); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);"></div>
        
        <span class="voice-3" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">What the pilot made clear</span>
        
        <h3 class="voice-1" style="max-width: 760px; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-md); line-height: 1.15; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">
          The pilot also brought important questions about materials, pacing, technology, financial content and continued implementation into clearer view.
        </h3>
        
        <p class="voice-2" style="max-width: 500px; color: var(--color-muted-slate); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
          Those lessons are informing what Ethnoir retains, changes and tests next.
        </p>
        
        <a href="/our-work" class="btn-primary" style="background-color: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain);">View Our Work &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 06: THE CHECK-IN -->
  <section class="bg-quiet-sand chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container two-columns">
      <div class="editorial-image-container">
        <img src="/images/check-in.jpg" alt="A premium notebook on a textured desk representing readiness" class="editorial-image" style="aspect-ratio: 4/3; object-fit: cover;" />
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; padding-left: var(--space-md);">
        <span class="voice-3">Venture Readiness Check-In</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">
          Unsure what deserves attention in your business right now?
        </h2>
        <p class="voice-2">
          The Venture Readiness Check-In is a short resource for people who have begun testing an idea with customers or are actively operating a business.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
          It asks you to reflect on customer activity, revenue, operations, financial visibility, repeatability and your capacity to carry the work. The result offers a starting point for considering which area may deserve attention next.
        </p>
        
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-sm); align-items: flex-start;">
          <a href="/venture-readiness-check-in" class="btn-primary" style="background: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain);">
            Explore the Check-In &rarr;
          </a>
          <span style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">
            This is not a funding decision, program application, business diagnosis or grade.
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 07: FOUNDER -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-moderate-spacing">
    <div class="container two-columns" style="align-items: center;">
      <div>
        <span class="voice-3">Founded by</span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">Olajumoke Michael</h2>
        <p class="voice-2">
          Olajumoke Michael founded Ethnoir in 2025 in Winston-Salem, North Carolina.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2">
          Her professional experience spans entrepreneurship support, program strategy and delivery, institutional operations, stakeholder coordination and program learning across nonprofit, higher-education, government and economic-development settings.
        </p>
        <div style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">
          <a href="/about" class="link-secondary">About Ethnoir &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="editorial-image-container" style="max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <img src="/images/ola.jpeg" alt="Olajumoke Michael, Founder of Ethnoir" class="editorial-image" style="aspect-ratio: 4/5; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top;" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 08: THE INSTITUTIONAL INVITATION -->
  <section class="bg-tidal-ink chapter chapter-large-spacing">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 960px;">
      <h2 class="voice-1" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); padding-bottom: var(--space-md); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
        Start with the challenge, not a predetermined service.
      </h2>
      <div class="two-columns">
        <div>
          <p class="voice-2">
            If your organization is trying to understand the conditions affecting entrepreneurs or examine a question arising from how venture support is designed, delivered or directed, Ethnoir welcomes the conversation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="voice-2">
            Share the question, decision or support challenge you are working through. From there, we can determine whether Ethnoir may be a useful fit.
          </p>
          <div class="actions-group">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">
              Discuss a venture-development challenge
            </a>
            <a href="/our-work" class="link-secondary">
              View Our Work
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER 09: THE FINAL CHOICE -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-tight-spacing">
    <div class="container" style="text-align: center; max-width: 600px;">
      <h3 class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">
        Navigating a venture yourself?
      </h3>
      <p class="voice-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
        The Venture Readiness Check-In offers another place to begin.
      </p>
      <a href="/venture-readiness-check-in" class="link-secondary">
        Explore the Check-In &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
